  "interpretation": [
    "All eight original C4 invocations fail; no assertion or deadline was weakened. Initial authority calls are usually short. The refined probe records completed writer waits up to 1608 ms, while entry-authority rebase maxima are 13/34/26/98 ms across its four invocations.",
    "SQL-worker queue medians are zero in all four refined invocations; p95 values are 425/139/258/83 ms. Queue tails can contribute, but these captures do not establish continuous worker-queue saturation.",
    "Owned submission and settlement remain additional costs: phase p95 values reach 743 and 1457 ms respectively. These overlap broader operations and some physical work continues after response expiry. Per-phase statistics include setup/diagnostic teardown; they are not successful business-request latency or constrained performance percentiles.",
    "Writer ownership includes callback checkpoints and producer finalization. Long teardown ownership spans are not used to infer live request cost. The captures do not prove a missed wake or authorize changing retry rules, command identities, clocks or ownership.",
    "Next owning investigation: reduce measured same-cell write/persistence/finalization work within the existing authority, contiguous-apply, exact-receipt and required S3 boundaries; qualify against the complete unchanged C2/C4 and exact-drain tests. Existing held-consumer regression already permits another producer on the same Queue, so it cannot substitute for the failing immediate-consumer load."
  ],
